R e a d m e
-----------

Switches your ship's systems between two states:

- Docked: batteries recharge, hydrogen tanks stockpile, and thrusters,
  gyroscopes, reactors, hydrogen engines, O2/H2 generators, beacons, ore
  detectors, and lights turn off.
- Flight: the same systems turn on, batteries go to Auto, and tanks stop
  stockpiling.

Antennas are never switched, so scripts that talk over antenna keep working
while docked. Add a [launchcontrol] override to an antenna to change that.

Docking is automatic. Connect your dock port and the ship shuts down.
Launching is the only thing you press.

SETUP
-----------

1. Load this script into a Programmable Block. It creates a [launchcontrol]
   section in the PB's Custom Data with defaults that work as-is.
2. Put the PB on your toolbar with the Run action and no argument.

If the ship has one connector, it is the dock port. With several, mark the
dock port by adding [launchcontrol] to its name or this to its Custom Data:
[launchcontrol]
dock_port=true
Nothing happens until a dock port is known.

LAUNCHING
-----------

Run the PB with no argument, or with launch. The script checks hydrogen,
battery charge, and that thrusters and gyroscopes are working. If anything
fails, the launch is refused and the reason is shown. Fix it or run
launch --force to skip the checks.

When the checks pass, flight systems come on, the dock port releases after a
short delay, and you are in Flight. If the port has not released within two
seconds the launch is reported as failed; flight systems stay on. Running dock
during a launch cancels it.

DISPLAYS AND LIGHTS
-----------

Add [launchcontrol] to the name of an LCD or cockpit. Its display_0 is set to
status. Add a key for any other screen that should show the dashboard:
[launchcontrol]
display_0=status
display_2=status
The PB's own screens take the same keys in the PB section. Run 'config' to
list which display_<n> keys each block has screens for.

show_title=false in a block's section drops the script title line from its
screens, for a screen whose job is already obvious from where it is.

The dashboard shows a status lamp, hydrogen and battery gauges with the launch
minimum marked, thruster and gyroscope counts, and any issues.

Add [launchcontrol] to a light's name, or set status_light=true in its Custom
Data. The light is never turned off and shows green Docked, blue Flight,
yellow blinking while launching or docking, red blinking when a launch is
blocked or failed, white in Manual.

PB CONFIGURATION
-----------

launch_delay_seconds=0.5   Between powering up and releasing.
dock_delay_seconds=0.5     Between connecting and shutting down.
min_hydrogen_percent=40    Launch needs at least this much.
min_battery_percent=40     Launch needs at least this much.
                           These are launch gates, not warning levels: below
                           them the launch is refused. Raise them if you want
                           a fuller ship before every launch.
auto_dock=true             false stops the automatic shutdown on connection.
auto_recover=true          false stops flight systems coming back on if the
                           ship disconnects without launching.
show_title=true            Whether this block's screens carry the script
                           title line.
display_0= display_1=      Roles for the PB's own screens. Add the ones you
                           want; they are not written for you.

Settings with a default are written into Custom Data on first run. Settings
that only matter when you set them, such as unused display_<n> keys and the
block overrides below, stay absent until you add them. Missing keys are
restored, invalid values fall back with a warning, and malformed INI is left
untouched while defaults are used. Edits are picked up within about ten
seconds or on any command.

BLOCK OVERRIDES
-----------

A block opts in by carrying the name tag or a [launchcontrol] section in its
Custom Data:
[launchcontrol]
ignore=false
docked=off
flight=on

ignore=true leaves the block alone entirely. docked and flight set what the
block does in each state: on, off, or ignore. Batteries also accept recharge,
auto, and discharge. Hydrogen and oxygen tanks also accept stockpile and auto.
Leave a key out to inherit the built-in rule for the block's type; the script
does not write them for you. Overrides work on any block, including ones the
script does not manage by default.

Cockpits, remote controls, timers, event controllers, button panels, the PB,
and connectors are never switched.

COMMANDS
-----------

launch           Check systems, power up, release the dock port. Default.
launch --force   Skip the checks. Also restores flight systems if the ship is
                 already free.
dock             Shut down into Docked. Runs automatically on connection.
dock --force     Shut down even if the dock port is not connected.
restore          Re-apply the systems for the current state.
manual / auto    Stop / resume managing systems.
status           Print the current state.
config           Print the active settings.
help             List commands.

NOTES
-----------

- Only blocks on this grid and its rotor, hinge, and piston subgrids are
  managed. Blocks on the grid you dock to are never touched.
- If the grid you dock to has no working power source, batteries stay on
  Auto instead of Recharge so the ship does not go dark.
- The state is read from the dock port whenever the script starts, so
  recompiling or reloading the world does not change any systems.
- Recompiling leaves Manual mode.
- FleetTelemetry measures fullness with the same shared code, so the two
  scripts never disagree about a number. Neither reads the other's state.
